<title>GERMANY: Hornbach dismisses takeover talk.</title>
<headline>Hornbach dismisses takeover talk.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German building store chain Hornbach Baumarkt AG on Monday said a newspaper report that it was a takeover target of Britain's Kingfisher group was unfounded.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that its majority shareholders, the Hornbach family, had no plans to sell its shares and was not in talks with Kingfisher.</p>
<p>Britain's Mail on Sunday had reported that Kingfisher was planning to take over the Hornbach group for around 400 million pounds.</p>
<p>Hornbach also said it had held negotiations in 1992 to place a minority stake with Kingfisher, but the talks had failed and the company had instead floated 20 percent of its equity on the German stock market.</p>
</text>
